('a197a7c7-622c-540e-b4d3-591d2db27aba'::uuid,'2108b48d-63ed-5be3-bdb5-2d1bdabb3811'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# INSTITUTIONAL IMPLEMENTATION PACKAGE\n\nThis package gives operational effect to Chapter 1 through a coordinated set of proposed legislative and executive instruments, standard operating procedures, responsibility matrices and governance templates. It is an integrated annex set and must be read with Chapter 1, particularly Sections 6–8, 11–14.\n\n# DOCUMENT CONTROL AND APPROVAL\n\n| **Control field**         | **Designation / entry**                                | **Control field**             | **Designation / entry**           |\n|---------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n| **Document owner**        | CDRRMO Head                                            | **Document custodian**        | CDRRMO Secretariat                |\n| **Technical review**      | CDRRMO / EOC / concerned offices                       | **Legal review**              | City Legal Office                 |\n| **Administrative review** | HRMO / Budget / Accounting / BAC                       | **External technical review** | OCD Region VIII, as applicable    |\n| **Approval**              | Mayor / CDRRMC / Sanggunian, as legally applicable     | **Effective date**            | Upon valid approval / issuance    |\n| **Review cycle**          | Annual and upon material legal or institutional change | **Supersedes**                | None – initial consolidated draft |\n\n## Revision history\n\n| **Version** | **Date**    | **Description**                                                                                     | **Prepared / reviewed by**            |\n|-------------|-------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|\n| 0.9         | 31 Oct 2026 | Integrated working draft based on uploaded Chapter 1 and assessment-informed implementation package | Prepared for institutional validation |\n\nApproval status: This document is a controlled working draft. No provision becomes an official City policy, ordinance, executive order or operational directive until approved and issued by the authority legally competent to do so.\n\n# Annex register and cross-reference guide\n\n| **Annex** | **Instrument**                                               | **Approval / control route**           |\n|-----------|--------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|\n| 1-A       | Proposed CDRRMO institutionalization ordinance               | Sangguniang Panlungsod                 |\n| 1-B       | Proposed CDRRMC reconstitution Executive Order               | City Mayor                             |\n| 1-C       | Proposed EOC establishment Executive Order                   | City Mayor                             |\n| 1-D       | SOP GOV-04: State of Calamity declaration and lifting        | Approval under City delegation         |\n| 1-E       | SOP GOV-05: State of Imminent Disaster / anticipatory action | Approval after RA 12287 IRR validation |\n| 1-F       | Master RACI and institutional interface matrix               | CDRRMC / City approval                 |\n| 1-G       | Governance forms GOV-F01 to GOV-F16                          | CDRRMO Secretariat custodian           |\n\nConsistent definitions. CDRRMC means City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council; CDRRMO means permanent City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office; EOC means Emergency Operations Center as an operational coordination mechanism; ICS means Incident Command System; IMT means Incident Management Team; PDRA means Pre-Disaster Risk Assessment; RDANA means Rapid Damage Assessment and Needs Analysis. These definitions are descriptive and do not confer authority beyond applicable law.\n\nDocument hierarchy. Philippine statutes and valid implementing rules prevail over administrative issuances, local executive issuances, approved plans, SOPs and forms. RACI designations allocate work but do not create statutory powers or transfer mandates.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1_00_package_control.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('29770c8d-1104-5794-b2da-cf2a34b631b2'::uuid,'07c8c36f-3092-5f21-8bb0-5df842023f5c'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# ANNEX 1-A \\| PROPOSED ORDINANCE – CDRRMO INSTITUTIONALIZATION\n\n**PROPOSED – FOR LEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW**\n\nDocument status: Draft instrument. This text is a drafting aid and must be checked against the latest certified statutes, implementing rules, local organizational structure, approved plantilla, budget, and applicable City procedures before signature or enactment.\n\n## AN ORDINANCE ESTABLISHING AND STRENGTHENING THE CITY DISASTER RISK REDUCTION AND MANAGEMENT OFFICE OF ORMOC CITY, DEFINING ITS ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE, FUNCTIONS AND ACCOUNTABILITY, PROVIDING FOR COORDINATION WITH THE CDRRMC AND EOC, AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES\n\nBE IT ORDAINED by the Sangguniang Panlungsod of Ormoc City, in session assembled, that:\n\n## Section 1. Short Title.\n\nThis Ordinance shall be known as the “Ormoc City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office Institutionalization Ordinance.”\n\n## Section 2. Declaration of Policy.\n\nThe City shall maintain a permanent, adequately staffed, technically competent and accountable CDRRMO consistent with RA 10121, its IRR, JMC No. 2014-1 and applicable local government, civil service and budget rules.\n\n## Section 3. Establishment and Status.\n\nThe CDRRMO is hereby established or, if already established by prior valid issuance, strengthened and institutionalized as a regular office of the City Government. The City Legal Office shall determine whether this is a new or amendatory ordinance after reviewing existing issuances.\n\n## Section 4. Organizational Structure.\n\nThe CDRRMO shall be headed by a duly qualified CDRRMO Head and maintain the functional areas required by applicable national guidelines: Administration and Training; Research and Planning; and Operations and Warning. Additional units and positions require approval under DBM, CSC and City processes.\n\n## Section 5. Functions.\n\nThe CDRRMO shall lead and coordinate local DRRM planning and implementation; risk information; contingency planning; early warning; training; preparedness; response coordination; recovery support; CDRRMC Secretariat functions; reporting; and institutional performance improvement, consistent with RA 10121.\n\n## Section 6. Relationship with CDRRMC and EOC.\n\nThe CDRRMC remains the City''s statutory policy-making, coordinating and oversight body. The CDRRMO is its permanent technical and administrative office. The EOC is an operational coordination mechanism established through a separate executive issuance. It does not replace the CDRRMO or field ICS command.\n\n## Section 7. Coordination and non-duplication.\n\nThe CDRRMO shall coordinate with City offices, barangays, national agencies, utilities, CSOs and private-sector partners, but shall not assume technical, regulatory, fiduciary or statutory functions assigned to other offices.\n\n## Section 8. Staffing and qualifications.\n\nHRMO and CDRRMO shall prepare staffing, qualification standards and position descriptions for review under applicable CSC and DBM rules. No position is created beyond an approved plantilla and lawful appropriation.\n\n## Section 9. Funding.\n\nFunding shall be sourced from lawful appropriations and eligible DRRM funds, subject to RA 10121, LDRRMF guidelines, budgeting, accounting, procurement and audit rules. This Ordinance does not independently authorize a particular allocation or expenditure.\n\n## Section 10. Implementing procedures.\n\nThe CDRRMO shall maintain the CDRRMO–EOC Manual of Operations and implementing procedures, subject to legal review and approval by the competent authority.\n\n## Section 11. Separability.\n\nIf any provision is declared invalid, the remaining provisions shall remain effective.\n\n## Section 12. Repealing / amending clause.\n\nInconsistent local issuances are amended or repealed only to the extent of inconsistency, subject to identification by the City Legal Office.\n\n## Section 13. Effectivity.\n\nThis Ordinance shall take effect in accordance with the Local Government Code and applicable approval, posting and publication requirements.\n\nDONE in Ormoc City, Philippines, this \\_\\_\\_\\_ day of \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ 20\\_\\_\\_\\_.  \n  \n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_  \nPRESIDING OFFICER / VICE MAYOR\n\nCERTIFIED CORRECT: \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ Secretary to the Sanggunian  \nAPPROVED, if required by law: \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ City Mayor\n\nLEGAL REVIEW: Confirm whether an existing ordinance already establishes the CDRRMO; determine new versus amendatory route; align structure and plantilla with JMC 2014-1, DBM/CSC rules; add fiscal note and identify affected prior issuances.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1-A.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('532825c5-033c-5bc8-a209-1a4c41bb6e6b'::uuid,'eee45c0c-b84d-5f47-ad35-0d4fab001f7c'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# ANNEX 1-B \\| PROPOSED EXECUTIVE ORDER – CDRRMC\n\n**PROPOSED – FOR LEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW**\n\nDocument status: Draft instrument. This text is a drafting aid and must be checked against the latest certified statutes, implementing rules, local organizational structure, approved plantilla, budget, and applicable City procedures before signature or enactment.\n\n## EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. \\_\\_\\_\\_ SERIES OF 20\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n## RECONSTITUTING THE ORMOC CITY DISASTER RISK REDUCTION AND MANAGEMENT COUNCIL, UPDATING ITS MEMBERSHIP AND ALTERNATES, AND PRESCRIBING ITS GOVERNANCE AND SECRETARIAT ARRANGEMENTS\n\nWHEREAS, RA 10121 and its IRR provide for local DRRM councils and their functions; WHEREAS, the City requires updated representation, regular deliberation and documented follow-through; NOW, THEREFORE, I, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, City Mayor of Ormoc City, hereby order:\n\n## Section 1. Reconstitution.\n\nThe CDRRMC is reconstituted in accordance with Section 11 of RA 10121 and its IRR. The final membership shall be listed in Schedule A, completed and legally checked before signature.\n\n## Section 2. Membership and alternates.\n\nEach member institution shall designate a principal and alternate in writing. CDRRMO shall verify all statutory seats, including required accredited CSO representation and private-sector representation, against the Act and IRR.\n\n## Section 3. Functions.\n\nThe Council shall exercise statutory policy, coordination, recommendation, plan review, resource oversight and monitoring functions.\n\n## Section 4. Meetings.\n\nThe Council shall meet at least once every three months and as necessary, consistent with applicable rules.\n\n## Section 5. Secretariat.\n\nThe CDRRMO shall serve as Secretariat and maintain meeting notices, agendas, technical papers, attendance, minutes, resolutions, decision register and action-monitoring reports.\n\n## Section 6. Decision authority.\n\nCouncil recommendations shall be distinguished from decisions reserved by law to the Mayor, Sanggunian or another competent authority.\n\n## Section 7. Working groups and inclusion.\n\nTechnical working groups may be established with terms of reference. CSO, private-sector, barangay and sector participation shall be meaningful and consistent with statutory composition.\n\n## Section 8. Effectivity.\n\nThis Order shall take effect upon signature, subject to applicable law.\n\n| **Schedule A – statutory / institutional seat** | **Principal**                                    | **Alternate** | **Designation / accreditation reference** |\n|-------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|---------------|-------------------------------------------|\n| City Mayor / Chairperson                        | \\[Name\\]                                         | \\[Name\\]      |                                           |\n| Other statutory City offices                    | \\[Complete per RA 10121 / IRR\\]                  |               |                                           |\n| National government agencies                    | \\[Complete per RA 10121 / IRR\\]                  |               |                                           |\n| Accredited CSO representatives                  | \\[At least four, subject to legal verification\\] |               |                                           |\n| Private-sector representative(s)                | \\[Complete\\]                                     |               |                                           |\n| Other prescribed members                        | \\[Complete\\]                                     |               |                                           |\n\nDONE in Ormoc City, Philippines, this \\_\\_\\_\\_ day of \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ 20\\_\\_\\_\\_.  \n  \n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_  \nCITY MAYOR\n\nLEGAL REVIEW: Verify exact statutory seats, CSO accreditation/selection, private-sector membership, alternates, quorum, voting and chair/vice-chair arrangement. Identify prior EO numbers and whether amended or superseded.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1-B.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('3252e77f-e003-5ad7-8678-fa69f3aeb2e0'::uuid,'ea2a9893-b34d-56d4-b144-106afe26ed06'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# ANNEX 1-C \\| PROPOSED EXECUTIVE ORDER – CITY EOC\n\n**PROPOSED – FOR LEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW**\n\nDocument status: Draft instrument. This text is a drafting aid and must be checked against the latest certified statutes, implementing rules, local organizational structure, approved plantilla, budget, and applicable City procedures before signature or enactment.\n\n## EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. \\_\\_\\_\\_ SERIES OF 20\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n## ESTABLISHING AND OPERATIONALIZING THE ORMOC CITY EMERGENCY OPERATIONS CENTER, DEFINING ITS FUNCTIONS, ACTIVATION AND DEACTIVATION, AND CLARIFYING ITS INTERFACE WITH THE CDRRMC, CDRRMO AND INCIDENT COMMAND SYSTEM\n\nWHEREAS, RA 10121 requires effective local DRRM coordination; WHEREAS, the City requires a defined operational coordination mechanism; WHEREAS, EOC coordination must not displace CDRRMC/CDRRMO mandates or ICS incident command; NOW, THEREFORE, I, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, City Mayor, hereby order:\n\n## Section 1. Establishment.\n\nThe City EOC is established as an operational coordination mechanism administered by the CDRRMO and activated under approved triggers and procedures.\n\n## Section 2. Functions.\n\nThe EOC maintains situational awareness; validates and disseminates incident information; supports executive and CDRRMC decision-making; coordinates resource requests; facilitates inter-office and inter-agency coordination; maintains incident and decision records; and supports transition to recovery.\n\n## Section 3. Non-command status.\n\nThe EOC is not a field command structure. The Incident Commander retains incident-level command under applicable ICS arrangements. EOC coordination does not alter agency mandates or operational control.\n\n## Section 4. Management.\n\nThe CDRRMO Head oversees readiness. A designated EOC Manager manages activated operations under approved job action sheets and reporting lines.\n\n## Section 5. Activation.\n\nActivation may be triggered by official warnings, PDRA findings, actual or imminent impacts, multi-barangay incidents, critical service disruption, resource coordination needs or direction of the Mayor / authorized official. The MOO shall specify levels and authority.\n\n## Section 6. Deactivation.\n\nThe authorized official shall deactivate the EOC when coordination needs have sufficiently reduced and transition arrangements are established. Closure includes logs, resource reconciliation and after-action review.\n\n## Section 7. Readiness and continuity.\n\nThe CDRRMO shall maintain duty rosters, contact directories, handover procedures, communications redundancy, facility checklists and minimum staffing arrangements, subject to approved resources.\n\n## Section 8. Information and records.\n\nThe EOC shall maintain incident logs, situation reports, decision logs, resource records and dashboards subject to privacy, security, records and disclosure requirements.\n\n## Section 9. Resources and effectivity.\n\nImplementation is subject to approved staffing, appropriations and procurement rules. This Order takes effect upon signature.\n\nDONE in Ormoc City, Philippines, this \\_\\_\\_\\_ day of \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ 20\\_\\_\\_\\_.  \n  \n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_  \nCITY MAYOR\n\nLEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW: Verify NDRRMC MC No. 131, s. 2018 title and current status with OCD Region VIII; identify any existing City EOC issuance; confirm activation/deactivation authority, staffing, facility and ICS/IMT reporting lines.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1-C.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('aa041bd5-cd72-5bc2-abe1-d5cccdbc4da7'::uuid,'e715b34c-ec5f-5f4c-b34c-378225a2156c'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# ANNEX 1-D \\| SOP GOV-04 – STATE OF CALAMITY\n\n**PROPOSED – FOR LEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW**\n\nDocument status: Draft instrument. This text is a drafting aid and must be checked against the latest certified statutes, implementing rules, local organizational structure, approved plantilla, budget, and applicable City procedures before signature or enactment.\n\n## STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE GOV-04: STATE OF CALAMITY DECLARATION, IMPLEMENTATION AND LIFTING\n\nPurpose. To establish a documented procedure consistent with Section 16 of RA 10121 and its IRR.\n\nCritical authority rule. The local sanggunian declares or lifts a State of Calamity upon recommendation of the LDRRMC, based on damage assessment and needs analysis. A Mayor''s Executive Order shall not substitute for the Sanggunian''s statutory declaration.\n\n| **Control**        | **Requirement**                                                                                                                               |\n|--------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Process owner      | CDRRMO Head                                                                                                                                   |\n| Recommendation     | CDRRMC, based on validated assessment                                                                                                         |\n| Decision authority | Sangguniang Panlungsod, as provided by law                                                                                                    |\n| Core evidence      | RDANA; affected population; casualties; infrastructure / livelihood damage; service interruption; urgent needs; response capacity             |\n| Records            | Assessment, Council minutes / recommendation, Sanggunian resolution, implementation and resource records, lifting recommendation / resolution |\n\n### Procedure\n\nReceive and log reports from BDRRMCs, response agencies, utilities and City offices; record source, time, location and verification status.\n\n1\\. Receive and log reports from BDRRMCs, response agencies, utilities and City offices; record source, time, location and verification status.\n\n2\\. Conduct and consolidate RDANA using approved methodology and competent sector offices; distinguish verified facts, estimates and information gaps.\n\n3\\. Prepare a technical assessment describing scale, severity, affected sectors, urgent needs, available capacity and basis for or against recommending declaration.\n\n4\\. Submit assessment to CDRRMC for deliberation and recommendation where statutory criteria are met.\n\n5\\. Transmit complete recommendation and evidence package to the Sangguniang Panlungsod for action through the legally prescribed process.\n\n6\\. Upon valid Sanggunian resolution, implement authorized remedial measures, assistance and reporting.\n\n7\\. Maintain post-declaration action register and monitor impacts, service restoration, resources and outstanding needs.\n\n8\\. When warranted, recommend lifting; the Sanggunian shall act through the applicable legal process.\n\n9\\. Archive the decision trail and conduct an after-action review.\n\nRequired records: incident report; RDANA; CDRRMC attendance, minutes and recommendation; Sanggunian resolution; action and resource register; public information; lifting recommendation and resolution. CLO shall verify statutory criteria, current IRR, resolution form, publication/posting and lifting process.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1-D.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('e0f13a3a-2df6-54bb-a514-03ceebc02c23'::uuid,'f66e432b-487f-5434-a8eb-de42ef848a67'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# ANNEX 1-E \\| SOP GOV-05 – STATE OF IMMINENT DISASTER\n\n**PROPOSED – FOR LEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW**\n\nDocument status: Draft instrument. This text is a drafting aid and must be checked against the latest certified statutes, implementing rules, local organizational structure, approved plantilla, budget, and applicable City procedures before signature or enactment.\n\n## STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE GOV-05: STATE OF IMMINENT DISASTER DECLARATION, ANTICIPATORY ACTION, LIFTING AND POST-LIFTING REPORTING\n\nPurpose. To establish a controlled process under RA 12287 and its certified IRR for PDRA, regional recommendation, local declaration, anticipatory action, lifting and reporting.\n\nCritical authority rule. A forecast alone does not automatically justify declaration. Statutory criteria, PDRA requirements and prescribed recommendation / coordination mechanism must be met. The Mayor''s declaration authority shall be exercised only after all legal prerequisites are confirmed.\n\n| **Control**              | **Requirement**                                                                                            |\n|--------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Process owner            | CDRRMO Head                                                                                                |\n| Technical lead           | CDRRMO Operations and Warning with sector offices                                                          |\n| Regional interface       | OCD Region VIII / RDRRMC VIII, subject to certified IRR                                                    |\n| Local decision authority | City Mayor, through EO only after prescribed recommendation                                                |\n| Funding                  | Budget / Accounting / Procurement subject to certified IRR and DBM / COA rules                             |\n| Reporting                | Post-lifting deadline as prescribed by certified IRR; 45 days reported in assessment and must be confirmed |\n\n### Procedure\n\n1\\. Monitor official forecasts and advisories from PAGASA, PHIVOLCS and other competent authorities; log source, issue time, validity, geography and lead time.\n\n2\\. Initiate PDRA when hazard-specific triggers warrant; assess exposure, vulnerability, projected severity, cascading impacts, sectoral needs, critical facilities, lead time and response capacity.\n\n3\\. Obtain sector inputs from health, social welfare, agriculture, engineering, utilities, education, transport, environment and barangays as relevant.\n\n4\\. Prepare PDRA summary, proposed anticipatory measures, resource requirements, funding source, implementation owners, safeguards and indicators.\n\n5\\. Convene CDRRMC or its authorized mechanism to review evidence and endorse the City''s request, without substituting for the statutory regional recommendation.\n\n6\\. Coordinate with OCD Region VIII / RDRRMC VIII through the certified IRR route; log request, attachments, receipt, clarifications, recommendation and official response.\n\n7\\. After confirmation of prerequisites, prepare the Mayor''s EO specifying hazard, covered areas, validity, authorized measures, responsible offices, resource controls and reporting.\n\n8\\. Implement only approved and legally authorized actions, which may include prepositioning, early evacuation, critical infrastructure protection, continuity measures and targeted assistance.\n\n9\\. Maintain action logs, beneficiary records, procurement and disbursement records, coverage, outputs, complaints and safeguards. Apply RA 10173 safeguards.\n\n10\\. Monitor hazard and impacts; lift the declaration in the manner prescribed by law and document basis, effective time and transition arrangements.\n\n11\\. Prepare and submit required post-lifting report within deadline in certified IRR; assessment records a 45-day period, which must be verified.\n\n12\\. Conduct after-action review and update triggers, PDRA tools, SOP and corrective action register.\n\nMandatory hold points: CLO verifies certified RA 12287 IRR and recommendation route; OCD VIII confirms regional / provincial coordination applicability to Ormoc as an Independent Component City; Budget, Accounting, CLO and OCD verify reported allocation percentages and tranche rules against certified IRR and DBM/COA guidance; beneficiary data comply with RA 10173.\n\nRequired records: official forecast log; PDRA; sector inputs; CDRRMC records; regional request and acknowledgment; recommendation; Mayor''s EO; anticipatory action / expenditure logs; lifting documentation; post-lifting report; after-action review.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1-E.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('37957e8c-b1ea-5311-9e3e-6175b4cce95b'::uuid,'2ad29b21-b115-57cb-8bc8-cc638387a41e'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# ANNEX 1-F \\| MASTER RACI AND INSTITUTIONAL INTERFACE MATRIX\n\n**PROPOSED – FOR LEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW**\n\nDocument status: Draft instrument. This text is a drafting aid and must be checked against the latest certified statutes, implementing rules, local organizational structure, approved plantilla, budget, and applicable City procedures before signature or enactment.\n\n| **Code** | **Meaning** | **Application**                                                                        |\n|----------|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| R        | Responsible | Performs work and produces output.                                                     |\n| A        | Accountable | Owns result / decision; one A per activity, subject to collective statutory authority. |\n| C        | Consulted   | Provides required advice before decision.                                              |\n| I        | Informed    | Receives relevant information.                                                         |\n\nRACI does not create statutory authority, transfer legal mandates or override formal delegations. A collective statutory body remains accountable for its decisions.\n\n| **Activity**                         | **Accountable (A)**                         | **Responsible (R)**                   | **Consulted / informed** |\n|--------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|--------------------------|\n| Enact CDRRMO ordinance               | Sangguniang Panlungsod                      | CDRRMO                                | Mayor, CLO, HRMO, Budget |\n| Prepare CDRRMC EO                    | Mayor                                       | CDRRMO / Secretariat                  | CLO, CDRRMC              |\n| Maintain CDRRMC register             | CDRRMO Head                                 | Secretariat                           | CLO, Council             |\n| Prepare CDRRMC meetings              | CDRRMC                                      | Secretariat                           | CDRRMO, member offices   |\n| Monitor Council actions              | CDRRMC                                      | CDRRMO / Secretariat                  | Concerned offices        |\n| Prepare State of Calamity assessment | CDRRMO Head                                 | RDANA / sector teams                  | CDRRMC, CLO, Finance     |\n| Recommend State of Calamity          | CDRRMC                                      | CDRRMO supplies evidence              | Sanggunian, CLO          |\n| Declare / lift State of Calamity     | Sangguniang Panlungsod                      | Sanggunian Secretariat                | CDRRMC, Mayor, CLO       |\n| Prepare SID PDRA                     | CDRRMO Head                                 | Operations & Warning / sector offices | CDRRMC, CLO, Budget, OCD |\n| Submit SID request                   | Authority prescribed by certified IRR       | CDRRMO                                | OCD VIII, CLO            |\n| Regional recommendation              | Competent regional body under certified IRR | OCD / RDRRMC VIII secretariat         | City                     |\n| Issue local SID EO                   | Mayor                                       | CDRRMO prepares package               | CLO, Budget, CDRRMC      |\n| Implement anticipatory action        | Mayor / designated office as authorized     | Sector offices / CDRRMO coordination  | Budget, Accounting, OCD  |\n| Prepare post-lifting report          | CDRRMO Head                                 | CDRRMO / sector offices               | CLO, Budget, OCD         |\n| Maintain legal register              | CDRRMO Head                                 | Secretariat / records custodian       | CLO                      |\n| Annual governance review             | CDRRMC                                      | CDRRMO / Secretariat                  | CLO, HRMO, Budget, OCD   |\n\n| **Interface**                           | **Accountable owner**                        | **Responsible actors**         | **CDRRMO role**                                  |\n|-----------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| CDRA / CLUP integration                 | CPDO                                         | CPDO technical team            | CDRRMO provides risk evidence and DRR/CCA advice |\n| DRR/CCA project screening               | CPDO / Budget by function                    | CPDO and Budget                | CDRRMO provides risk-screening inputs            |\n| Critical facility structural assessment | City Engineer / Building Official            | Engineering / inspection teams | CDRRMO supports risk prioritization              |\n| Power, water, telecom continuity        | Utility provider / designated City authority | Utilities and relevant offices | CDRRMO coordinates information and priorities    |\n| Watershed / ecosystem monitoring        | CENRO / competent environment authority      | CENRO, DENR and partners       | CDRRMO integrates findings                       |\n| Health anticipatory action              | City Health Officer                          | CHO, hospitals and partners    | CDRRMO coordinates through EOC / cluster         |\n| Education continuity                    | DepEd Schools Division                       | School DRRM coordinators       | CDRRMO coordinates preparedness                  |\n| Agriculture / fisheries early action    | City Agriculture / Veterinary Office         | Sector offices and agencies    | CDRRMO coordinates hazard information            |\n| Price monitoring                        | DTI / City Market Office                     | Market monitoring personnel    | EOC information integration                      |\n| Business continuity outreach            | CDRRMO Head                                  | CDRRMO and Chamber of Commerce | Joint outreach; each retains own mandate         |\n\nAll office heads shall validate assignments. CDRRMO coordinates system-wide resilience but does not appropriate statutory or technical mandates belonging to other institutions.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1-F.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('df391a4d-2377-55d2-a59f-1c37ae577ad2'::uuid,'1a2135aa-84f2-5ac2-97ff-f5ba295fcf32'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# ANNEX 1-G \\| GOVERNANCE FORMS, TEMPLATES AND REGISTERS\n\n**PROPOSED – FOR LEGAL / TECHNICAL REVIEW**\n\nDocument status: Draft instrument. This text is a drafting aid and must be checked against the latest certified statutes, implementing rules, local organizational structure, approved plantilla, budget, and applicable City procedures before signature or enactment.\n\n| **Form code** | **Template / register**                          | **Minimum fields**                                                                                                                   |\n|---------------|--------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| GOV-F01       | CDRRMC Membership and Designation Register       | Statutory seat; institution; principal; alternate; designation date; CSO accreditation; contact; validity; verification.             |\n| GOV-F02       | CDRRMC Meeting Notice and Agenda                 | Meeting number; date/time/venue; convening authority; agenda; lead office; papers; distribution.                                     |\n| GOV-F03       | CDRRMC Attendance and Minutes                    | Attendance; quorum; agenda; discussion; decisions; dissent; action owner; deadline; approval.                                        |\n| GOV-F04       | CDRRMC Resolution Template                       | Resolution number/title; legal basis; findings; operative clauses; voting; certification.                                            |\n| GOV-F05       | Resolution and Action Monitoring Register        | Decision; action owner; deliverable; due date; status; evidence; escalation; closure.                                                |\n| GOV-F06       | Institutional Policy Review Checklist            | Legal authority; consistency; mandate; consultation; inclusion; privacy; staffing; budget; monitoring; legal clearance.              |\n| GOV-F07       | State of Calamity Technical Assessment           | Event; affected barangays; casualties; population; damage; livelihood; services; needs; capacity; evidence.                          |\n| GOV-F08       | State of Calamity Recommendation and Resolution  | RDANA; CDRRMC deliberation; recommendation; Sanggunian action; legal review; implementation / lifting.                               |\n| GOV-F09       | State of Imminent Disaster PDRA Summary          | Hazard; official source; forecast; lead time; geography; exposure; vulnerability; impacts; sector needs; actions; costs; safeguards. |\n| GOV-F10       | Request to RDRRMC VIII / OCD VIII                | Legal route; requesting authority; PDRA; action proposal; attachments; submission; acknowledgment; response.                         |\n| GOV-F11       | Mayor''s State of Imminent Disaster EO Template   | Recitals; legal basis; prerequisite recommendation; hazard / areas; actions; owners; resources; duration; reporting; lifting.        |\n| GOV-F12       | State of Imminent Disaster Lifting Documentation | Updated risk; basis; regional coordination; authority; lifting instrument; effective time; transition.                               |\n| GOV-F13       | Post-Lifting Report                              | Timeline; PDRA; actions; coverage; expenditure; beneficiaries; outputs; lessons; attachments; proof of submission.                   |\n| GOV-F14       | Institutional RACI Register                      | Process; activity; A; R; C; I; legal authority; approving authority; review date.                                                    |\n| GOV-F15       | Corrective and Preventive Action Register        | Finding; root cause; risk; action; owner; actors; resources; due date; evidence; effectiveness; closure.                             |\n| GOV-F16       | Legal and Policy Register                        | Instrument; authority; number/date; subject; status; official source; owner; implications; review date.                              |\n\nEvery controlled form shall display City Government of Ormoc, document code, version, date, page number, preparer, reviewer, approving authority where applicable, classification, records custodian and related SOP / Chapter reference. Personal information shall be collected only when necessary and processed under RA 10173.\n\n# FINAL INTEGRATION AND RELEASE CHECKLIST\n\n| **Validation subject**     | **Required action**                                                                                                                                   |\n|----------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| CDRRMO legal basis         | CLO to identify existing ordinances / EOs and determine new or amendatory legislative route.                                                          |\n| Structure and staffing     | HRMO / CDRRMO to align functions, plantilla and qualifications with JMC 2014-1 and current DBM / CSC rules.                                           |\n| CDRRMC membership          | Verify statutory seats, CSO accreditation / selection, private-sector representation, alternates, quorum and voting.                                  |\n| EOC basis                  | OCD VIII / CLO to verify national EOC guidance, existing City orders, activation authority and ICS interface.                                         |\n| State of Calamity          | CLO to validate RA 10121 Section 16, evidence criteria, Sanggunian action and lifting process.                                                        |\n| State of Imminent Disaster | CLO / OCD VIII to verify certified RA 12287 IRR, regional route, Ormoc ICC coordination, timelines and local EO prerequisites.                        |\n| Funding                    | Budget / Accounting / BAC / CLO to verify percentages, eligibility, tranche rules and procurement / disbursement against certified IRR and DBM / COA. |\n| Privacy and records        | DPO / ICT / Records Officer to validate beneficiary data, data sharing, retention, access and security.                                               |\n| Document consistency       | Secretariat to check annex codes, form codes, cross-references, register and revision history.                                                        |\n\nRelease condition: No draft instrument shall be signed, enacted, circulated as effective policy or used as the sole basis for expenditure until its legal route, factual schedules, delegated authority, budget implications and approval requirements have been confirmed.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/Annex_1-G.md (Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9, 31 Oct 2026)','draft')
